## Why This Is Asked

Gauges ability to design end-to-end CAPA artifacts for data exposure in multi-tenant data platforms.

## Key Concepts

- CAPA data modeling
- Lifecycle state machines
- API design for incident records
- Telemetry and tenant-scoped metrics
- RCA templates and Canary remediation

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal REST handler sketch for creating a CAPA
app.post('/caps', (req, res) => {
  const { cap_id, incident, tenant_id, evidence } = req.body;
  if (!cap_id || !tenant_id) return res.status(400).send('Missing fields');
  // store CAPA entry
  res.status(201).json({ cap_id, status: 'created' });
});
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test the CAPA under concurrent backup runs?
- What metrics would you monitor to ensure containment over time?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests a candidate's ability to design end-to-end CAPA for a security breach in a multi-region, multi-tenant system, including data modeling, lifecycle orchestration, API design, regional metrics, and a corrective/preventive path.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model with evidence, logs, IAM changes, tenant IDs, data lineage, PII risk tagging
- Region-aware lifecycle state machine for CAPA progress
- Idempotent REST API design to link evidence and traces
- Region/tenant metrics to prove containment and prevent recurrence
- RCA templates and canary-based prevention (policy rollback, tenant-scoped controls)

## Code Example
```javascript
interface CAPARecord {
  id: string;
  evidence: string[];
  accessLogs: string[];
  iamChanges: string[];
  tenantId: string;
  dataLineage: string;
  piiRisk: 'low'|'medium'|'high';
  region: string;
  status: 'detected'|'contained'|'eradicated'|'verified'|'closed';
  createdAt: string;
  updatedAt: string;
  linkedLogs?: string[];
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you ensure idempotency for the CAPA creation API?
- What data-retention/privacy policies apply to storing PII risk tags?
- How would you automate regional gates and rollback across tenants?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design end-to-end CAPA workflow for data privacy policy failures, including evidence capture and cross-tenant rollout.

## Key Concepts

- CAPA data modeling for evidence and artifacts
- Lifecycle state machine and ownership
- Minimal REST API design with linked logs/traces
- Tenant/region metrics for containment and recurrence
- RCA templates and canary rollout planning

## Code Example

```javascript
// CAPA core types (overview)
interface CAPA {
  id: string;
  title: string;
  evidence: string[];
  artifacts: string[];
  state: 'detected'|'triaged'|'in_progress'|'contained'|'closed';
  createdAt: string;
  updatedAt?: string;
  links?: { type: string; url: string }[];
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you scale CAPA data stores across regions?
- How to ensure regulatory auditability and evidence integrity?
